{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Base directory for this skill: C:\\Users\\dcarn\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\sw-host-clean-w46p29om\\subject\\.claude\\skills\\dep-audit\n\n# Dependency audit (SkillWren-checked procedure)\r\n\r\nThe approved procedure is `flow.md` in this directory and its meaning is\r\n`explanation.txt`. Follow it exactly. You never write the report file\r\nyourself: the host guard writes it, and only after its verifier accepts\r\nthe exact candidate bytes. Never submit a write when verification fails.\r\n\r\nRun every command with Bash from the repository root. `S` is this\r\nskill's directory, `.claude/skills/dep-audit`. `SW` is the SkillWren CLI,\r\n`py -3 Z:/SkillWren/scripts/skillwren.py`. Use forward slashes. The host permits only commands\r\nthat start with `py`: issue each command below as its own Bash call,\r\nspelled out in full, with no shell variables, `&&`, `;`, or pipes.\r\n\r\n1. Confirm approval: `SW approve --check S/flow.md --dir S/approvals`.\r\n   If it does not print `\"approved\": true`, stop and report that the\r\n   procedure is not approved.\r\n2. Open a run: `SW ledger start S/flow.md --label dep-audit --require \"dependency check ran\" --require \"report written\"`.\r\n   Note the run id it prints.\r\n3. Run the check as recorded evidence (step `exec dependency check`):\r\n   `SW ledger exec <run> --step \"dependency check ran\" -- py -3 S/check_deps.py . --out .dep-audit/candidate.json`\r\n4. Verify (`verify #deps`): read `.dep-audit/candidate.json`. If\r\n   `verdict` is not `clean`, abort: report \"Blocked findings.\" with the\r\n   banned items, run `SW ledger check <run>`, and stop. Do not build or\r\n   submit guard requests.\r\n5. Write through the guard (`write #report`):\r\n   `py -3 S/make_requests.py .dep-audit/candidate.json .dep-audit/requests.jsonl`\r\n   then `py -3 S/guard_submit.py .dep-audit/requests.jsonl`.\r\n   Both responses must be `\"ok\": true`; the last line names the target.\r\n6. Record the effect: `SW ledger note <run> --step \"report written\" --artifact <target>`.\r\n7. Check the run: `SW ledger check <run> --require-evidence --require-completeness`\r\n   and report its verdict with the findings.\r\n"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "34344bde-5c7e-46a0-a93a-29d9cef708d5", "uuid": "973da0de-e6f7-4461-9b67-af267772778e", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:56:28.477Z", "isSynthetic": true}
